{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_013jhk2W512jfZuzLDsr3ctK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## rnd-v1 â€” Build Trio Session Summary\n\n**Goal:** Build the Anchor R&D Control Surface foundation as a sequence of code-only waves (2â€“9), each gated GREEN and adversarially reviewed before advancing.\n\n**Grounded claims (per the execution log):**\n\n- **Wave 2 â€” Foundations:** Added `paths.py` (lazy `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`, `ensure_data_dirs()`, re-entrant `WRITE_LOCK`, `auth_ok()`/`expected_token()`, `bind_with_retry()`, idempotent `migrate_data()`); moved `anchor_gui.py` to `ThreadingHTTPServer` with `@_with_write_lock` on mutators and a token gate atop `do_POST`. GATE GREEN, 22 passed; GO after 1 fix iter (MINOR-1: import-time mkdir made lazy).\n\n- **Wave 3 â€” Registry + New-Project flow:** Added `rnd_registry.py` (id-keyed, non-unique `folder_path`, CRUD, `group_by_folder`, retain-not-delete lifecycle, per-project `.anchor/projects/<id>/{research,planning,build,deliverables,jobs}/` scaffold, idempotent legacy-id assignment) and `dir_browser.py` (stdlib server-side dir browser). `anchor_gui.py` gained the New-Project flow, `/project/<id>` route, and folder-grouped tiles with a 4-state status line. GO after 1 fix iter.\n\n- **Wave 4 â€” Durable-job keystone:** Added `job_runner.py` â€” `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`-indirected launch, durable per-job log + ring buffer (deque maxlen 5000), `long_poll(since, ceiling=25s)`, `cancel()` via `taskkill /T /F /PID`, and `reconcile_on_startup` â†’ `interrupted`; job store under `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR/rnd_jobs/` with atomic writes. Added `tests/fake_claude.py` deterministic mock. GO, 0 fix iters.\n\n- **Wave 5 â€” Gate adapter:** Added `gate_adapter.py` â€” parses stream-json into a prompt-box record (`question`, `options`, `tool_use_id`, `header`, `multiSelect`) with `mark_awaiting_input` persistence. The wave authored a faithful deterministic `gate_stream.jsonl` fixture (a real `AskUserQuestion` tool_use) since the captured one was absent; no live `claude`. GO after 1 fix iter.\n\n- **Wave 6 â€” Lane wiring + concurrency:** Added `lanes.py` (frozen lane map researchâ†’researchPrime / planâ†’Crucible / buildâ†’Foreman â†’ {skill, prompt-seed, output subdir, gate flag}; `launch_lane()` passes per-project output dir into the engine and writes a `launch.pointer.json` proof). `job_runner.py` gained a concurrency layer (`_ACTIVE_LANE` same-lane-serialize/cross-lane-concurrent; `_FOLDER_BUILD` build serialization). GO, 0 fix iters.\n\n- **Wave 7 â€” History + report viewer + cost rollup:** Added `effort_history.py` (job-id-scoped append-only pointer-records, index reversed on read [0 = newest], nothing deleted on re-run, cost capture, per-effortâ†’laneâ†’project rollups, scoped per-effort git auto-commit, no push) and `report_viewer.py` (PDF-by-default else stdlib mdâ†’HTML reader, traversal-safe). Vendored REAL KaTeX 0.16.11. GO after 1 fix iter.\n\n- **Wave 8 â€” Data-free distribution:** Added `distro.py` (deny-by-default manifest staging + no-personal-data scan), `dist_manifest.txt`, planted-secret fixtures. Initial GATE GREEN 117 passed, but **both reviewers returned NO-GO** â€” BLOCKER-1: a hard-coded real email literal would ship/leak PII; MAJOR-1: globally-exploitable `distro-scan: allow` self-grant marker; MAJOR-2: token scan missed unquoted secrets. (Fixes followed; resolved before terminal wave.)\n\n- **Wave 9 â€” Deliverables + taskâ†”project (TERMINAL):** Added `deliverables.py` with per-type success contracts (doc=exists+nonempty; script/skill=exit 0 + result-no-error; program=exit 0 within timeout) enforcing stdin=DEVNULL, non-interactive, timeout, and tree-kill reap. `anchor_gui.py` gained the project-tasks view + token-gated `link_task`/`run_deliverable`; `anchor.py` gained `link_task`/`link` CLI. GO, 0 fix iters.\n\n**Process pattern:** Every wave ran EXECUTE â†’ orchestrator-run GATE â†’ 2 independent refute-mode REVIEWs â†’ FIX â†’ JUDGE, with BLOCKER consensus (â‰¥2) required to halt. All model calls were stubbed (`fake_claude.py` / authored fixtures) â€” no live `claude`.\n\n**Findings/risks surfaced:** The Wave-8 distribution scanner was the one wave to draw a unanimous NO-GO â€” the security-relevant blockers (PII literal, self-suppression marker, unquoted-secret blind spot) were caught only by adversarial review, not the GREEN test gate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":94068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a22dda71-233e-4a4c-9e51-93689f2f3a55","uuid":"cbc01ab2-38e1-4dd8-b488-94cf0cba1d61","request_id":"req_011CcJoEjBWrDTnZ3jwjL6Qm"}
